  <!-- SEPARATION SIX. The authorings above are for couples THREE (Facing Couples Compact) and FOUR
       (Facing Couples, b1) apart; the heads of a Static Square are two couples facing each other SIX
       apart, so `Heads Right and Left Thru` - SIX of the first-call failures, the largest single
       group - matched neither. The law is the one every separation fix in this catalogue has used
       and the two authorings pin it: `scaleX = separation / 2`, so separation 6 gives
       `scaleX = 3` on the pull-by and the extension. `Beau Wheel`/`Belle Wheel` are NOT scaled:
       they are the courtesy turn taken at the end, not part of the travel. Everything else is
       unchanged, and the start formation is written INLINE at x = -3 so the engine's own mirror
       (180 degrees about the origin) puts the second couple at x = +3.

       MEASURED BLAST RADIUS, because this variant also lets the whole board tile (heads and sides
       are both facing-couple boxes, so bare `Right and Left Thru` becomes legal from a Static
       Square): legal calls from a Static Square 232 -> 233, i.e. exactly this one call; the figure
       suite's first-call failures 13 -> 7; and the motion keeps every couple 2.00 apart, so it does
       not touch the identity-coherence defect pinned in selection.mjs. -->
  <tam title="Right and Left Thru"
       from="Facing Couples"
       parts="3" difficulty="1" sequencer="no" formation="Facing Couples Far" vid="V1-bmfeupbe">
    <path>
      <move select="Pull Left" beats="1.5" scaleX="3" scaleY=".5" />
      <move select="Extend Right" beats="1.5" scaleX="3" scaleY=".5" />
      <move select="Beau Wheel" scaleX=".67" />
    </path>
    <path>
      <move select="Pull Left" beats="1.5" scaleX="3" scaleY=".5" />
      <move select="Extend Right" beats="1.5" scaleX="3" scaleY=".5" />
      <move select="Belle Wheel" scaleX=".67" />
    </path>
  </tam>

  <!-- SEPARATION TWO, for the Trade By boards. The authorings above are separations THREE (Facing
       Couples Compact) and SIX (the inline one), and the corpus's remaining `Right and Left Thru`
       refusals are on a Trade By whose facing couples are TWO apart - so both miss, and it is the
       largest remaining `no setup matches` group that is not a body error.

       Same law, same number as every other separation fix here: `scaleX = separation / 2` on the
       pull-by and the extension, so separation 2 gives `1`. `Beau Wheel`/`Belle Wheel` are NOT scaled
       (the courtesy turn at the end, not travel), and the start formation is written INLINE at x = -1
       so the engine's own mirror puts the second couple at x = +1.

       MEASURED: see PLAN.md. Authored, then the census and `verify-suite` decide - the same
       procedure as the `Box the Gnat` separation-6 tam, which is the one that has held. -->
  <tam title="Right and Left Thru"
